an apparent sea change in hong kong's  approach to covet 19. on monday its  chief executive kari lam announced the  city's border measures some of the  toughest in the world will finally be  relaxed a flight ban from nine countries  will be scrapped including the united  states the united kingdom india and  australia  this ban is no longer necessary because  the covenanted situation in these  countries is no worse than in hong kong  and many travelers coming here do not  have symptoms  quarantine will also be cut from 14 days  to one week for vaccinated travelers who  test negative  this only applies to residents tourists  are still unable to enter  plans to carry out city-wide testing are  also on hold  up until recently the city had been  pursuing a zero-tolerance policy to  stamping out the virus in line with  mainland china but that changed since  the number of cases increased  dramatically along with the death rate  no surprise because uh both the local  experts and also the uh experts from the  you know chinese cdc delegates we all in  nine uh of that  so we believe that we should focus on  increasing the vaccination rate  especially among the elderly  last week lamb conceded tolerance of the  severe measures was fading the tough  policy has also weighed on the economy  business leaders like alan zeeman have  warned the strict measures could have a  lasting impact on the city's status as a  financial hub  a host of other social distancing rules  are also set to be phased out in the  next month or so including the  two-person gathering limit and a dining  curfew  schools will go back to face-to-face  learning from next month a little bit of  the relax of the restriction is good  i don't agree with removing the flight  span covered 19 positive people are all  over the world if we allow people to  come here hong kong cannot deal with it  it's been a pain to all the hong kong  citizens i do feel relieved but  don't really trust the government that  much  i feel like she might change it again  soon lamb says the phasing out of social  distancing measures are dependent on  there being no resurgence of the virus  in the coming weeks and months brit  clinic al jazeera hong kong
 

